+ *  .6  A registered I_T nexus refused RESERVATION CONFLICT after its
+ *      session's re-login (measured 2026-10-23: every refused write of a
+ *      4 s path cut fell 6-14 ms after the login).  When an initiator logs
+ *      in again with the same ISID after the old session has started
+ *      shutting down, the login is a new session, and
+ *      scst_pr_init_tgt_dev() left the registrant on the old session's
+ *      tgt_dev until scst_free_session() freed it.  The new tgt_dev now
+ *      takes the registrant from a tgt_dev whose session is no longer
+ *      READY, and scst_pr_abort_reg() also aborts every other live
+ *      session of the registrant's nexus on the device, so commands the
